#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Chess: Full Quick Game Victory vs Computer AI on the Pirates 3D Theme (#303, #304).
#
# Reuses throne-room.route's boot -> Ada profile -> Throne Room -> Quick Game prefix (flips
# 290..431), switches the Quick Game theme from Western to Pirates via Choose Theme (320,65) while
# keeping Black as the Oxford Softworks Computer AI (default difficulty 25, matched Blue Soldiers
# vs Red Pirates sets, capture cartoons enabled), and plays a 26-move (51-ply) legal game with
# nine captures (triggering 3D Pirate capture cartoons) through to Checkmate ("Checkmate!
# Congratulations, you win!"), returning to the Throne Room via the green tick and closing cleanly.
#
# Replay with a fresh `--data-root <empty dir>`, never beside the rip: it reaches the New Player
# form only with no profile saved and writes profiles\prof1.lcp and profiles\1save.lcs.
#
# Landmarks (fresh --data-root, with GM16.DLS):
# - Boot & profile: flips 0..391 (New Player "Ada", "Who's playing?", Throne Room at flip 392).
# - Quick Game setup: flip 432 -> Choose Theme (320,65) -> Pirates at flip 440 -> Start (590,410)
#   at flip 450 (loads PIRATES.RES, staunton\ptune.mid, Advisors\admiral.avi & pirate.avi).
# - Active 3D gameplay window: flips 555..18800 (Pirates 3D board ready -> Checkmate victory).
# - Verified 3D Pirate capture cartoon landmarks:
#     * Pawn-vs-Pawn (3. exd5 & 3... exd5): flips ~1684..3084 (samples: 1984, 2584, 2884)
#     * Bishop-vs-Queen & Knight-vs-Bishop (8. Bxd7+ & 8... Nxd7): flips ~5614..7114 (samples: 5614, 6814)
#     * Bishop-vs-Knight (9. Bxe7): flips ~7560..8440 (sample: 7560)
#     * Queen-vs-Rook Checkmate (26. Qxa8#): flips ~18352..18652 (sample: 18352, iris wipe at 18652)
# - Full move sequence (White Human Blue Soldiers vs Black Computer AI Red Pirates):
#     1.  e2-e4     (flip 560..581)     1...  e7-e6
#     2.  d2-d4     (flip 936..957)     2...  d7-d5
#     3.  e4xd5     (flip 1362..1383)   3...  e6xd5   [Captures #1 & #2: Pawn-vs-Pawn cartoons]
#     4.  Qd1-h5    (flip 3148..3169)   4...  Qd8-d7
#     5.  Bf1-b5    (flip 3554..3575)   5...  Ke8-e7
#     6.  Bc1-g5+   (flip 4000..4021)   6...  Ke7-e8
#     7.  Qh5-e2+   (flip 4646..4667)   7...  Ng8-e7
#     8.  Bb5xd7+   (flip 5292..5313)   8...  Nb8xd7  [Captures #3 & #4: Bishop-vs-Queen & Knight-vs-Bishop cartoons]
#     9.  Bg5xe7    (flip 7238..7259)   9...  c7-c5   [Capture #5: Bishop-vs-Knight cartoon]
#    10.  Be7-d6+   (flip 8464..8485)  10...  Ke8-d8
#    11.  Bd6-e7+   (flip 8890..8911)  11...  Kd8-c7
#    12.  Nb1-c3    (flip 9366..9387)  12...  c5xd4   [Capture #6: Pawn-vs-Pawn cartoon]
#    13.  Nc3-b5+   (flip 10692..10713) 13... Kc7-c6
#    14.  Nb5xd4+   (flip 11118..11139) 14... Kc6-b6  [Capture #7: Knight-vs-Pawn cartoon]
#    15.  Qe2-b5+   (flip 12444..12465) 15... Kb6-c7
#    16.  Qb5-a5+   (flip 12870..12891) 16... b7-b6
#    17.  Nd4-b5+   (flip 13296..13317) 17... Kc7-c6
#    18.  a2-a4     (flip 13722..13743) 18... Nd7-e5
#    19.  Qa5-c3+   (flip 14148..14169) 19... Ne5-c4
#    20.  Nb5-d4+   (flip 14574..14595) 20... Kc6-b7
#    21.  Qc3-b4    (flip 15000..15021) 21... a7-a5
#    22.  Qb4-b5    (flip 15426..15447) 22... Nc4xb2  [Capture #8: Knight-vs-Pawn cartoon]
#    23.  Qb5-c6+   (flip 16752..16773) 23... Kb7-a7
#    24.  Nd4-b5+   (flip 17178..17199) 24... Ka7-a6
#    25.  Nb5-c7+   (flip 17604..17625) 25... Ka6-a7
#    26.  Qc6xa8#   (flip 18030..18051)               [Capture #9: Queen-vs-Rook cartoon -> Checkmate!]
# - Victory & clean exit: Checkmate dialog at flip 18800 -> green tick (320,232) at flip 18811
#   (poll 300 up) -> Throne Room return -> close at flip 18860 -> Exited(0).
